.\" Title: vrc-thaw
.\" Author: vrc contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRC\-THAW 1 "2025" "vrc" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrc\-thaw \- resume a frozen command in a running instance via SIGCONT

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrc
\fBthaw\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOMMAND\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Thaw (resume) a frozen command by sending it SIGCONT, allowing it to continue execution from where it was suspended by \fBvrc freeze\fR.

Connects to the target instance's UDS control socket at \fB~/.local/share/vrc/control\-{pid}.sock\fR and sends the thaw request.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B PID
OS process ID of the target vrc instance.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fICOMMAND\fR
ID of the target command (omit for the first/only command).

.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Present a numbered list of all frozen commands in the instance and allow the user to select one or more by number (space-separated). Only frozen commands are shown.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Resume the only command:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc thaw 12345\fR
Command cmd_abc thawed (SIGCONT)
.fi
.RE

.PP
Interactively select frozen commands to resume:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc thaw 12345 \-\-interactive\fR
  1) cargo build (PID 5678) - frozen for 5m 12s
  2) make test (PID 5680) - frozen for 1m 03s
Select [space-separated numbers]: 1 2
Command cmd_abc thawed (SIGCONT)
Command cmd_def thawed (SIGCONT)
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Command thawed successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Error (instance not found, command not found, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrc (1),
.BR vrc\-freeze (1),
.BR vrc\-list (1),
.BR kill (1)
